<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu al-Khattab al-Ma'afiri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 761</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu al-Khattab al-Ma'afiri was an Arab Ibadi leader elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> in 757 by the Ibadi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berbers</a> of Tripolitania and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nafusa-mountains">Jebel Nafusa</a>. His forces took Tripoli and in 758 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kairouan">Kairouan</a>, ending the rule of the Sufri Warfajuma there. An Abbasid army under Muhammad ibn al-Ash'ath defeated and killed him at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tawergha">Tawargha</a> in 761, ending his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imamate">imamate</a>.</p></div>
